Regarding support from DS (from Andrei Ilie):

{quote}
*TK:*
what about *speech-to-text* and *text-to-speech features* (integrated with in-app Chat)?
If we would like to use some solution which allows to be locally hosted (like Mozilla TTS / suno-ai bark / SpeechT5 / coqui), *what would be the estimated effort for DS to support us?*{quote}

{quote}*Andrei:*{quote}

{quote}DS could assist in the same way as we did for CS automations using OpenAI: while mostly engineering work, it was useful to build it in DS infra and provide (automatic) evaluation scripts to assess the quality with each new deployment or improvement attempt.I would say *12w for each on the DS side*, but could vary depending on certain factors:{quote}

{quote}it'd be best to have these models hosted in DS infra (provided by Models Lifecycle), as they provide nice to have tooling aimed to Machine Learning solutions (training and tuning if needed, monitoring and alerting if data distributions shift, is generally Python native, etc). However, either ENG or DS can built it in that infra. We've had ENGs building in the DS repo (and infra) in the past when the use case was a Machine Learning driven one. Depending on whether DS builds it or ENG builds it and DS just support, DS and ENG required capacities can vary quite a lot

we'll want to have good evaluation tooling to understand how well the solutions we host does. We'll want to have these as part of the model deployment process ran in an automatic way, but also quicker ways to run these locally for faster iterations (on e.g. different configs of the TTS and STT models). The caveat is we never worked with audio data, so there is no previous case of such validation in DS, but I don't see why it'd be a lot harder.{quote}

