As a platform service provider, Bolt is required by the Guidelines for the package delivery services provided by using motorcycles to do the followings:

(1)        Conduct criminal record checks on the Drivers and verify their driving licenses;
(2)        Provide training to drivers on driving safety and the speed limits as mandated by the law;
(3)        Refrain from launching any sales promotions that could encourage drivers to exceed speed limits mandated by the law or engage in criminal activities;
(4)        Ensure that all motorcycles comply with vehicle tax payments and possess proper insurance under the Vehicle Accident Protection Act B.E. 2535 (1992);
(5)        Verify that any boxes or instruments safely attached to the motorcycles are free from sharp parts or rough parts that may pose a danger to the drivers or other road users, and meet the qualifications specified in the DLT Notification re: the Qualifications, Size, and Installation of Boxes or Instruments for Motorcycles B.E. 2564 (2021);
(6)        Ensure that it has a system for collecting the information on the packages and the name and the address of the Client, and a policy or a warning in place in relation to illegal items;
(7)        Immediately report the Royal Thai Police or the Office of the Narcotics Control Board whenever there is any suspect illegal items or narcotics in the delivery package;
(8)        Ensure that there is a policy in place to handle accidents and emergency incidents;
(9)        Cooperate with the DLT in providing information and documents, including contact details of the contact person; and
(10)    Annually, submit the details of drivers and their driving licenses to the DLT by e-mail.



